## Professional Vocabulary 
* Cloud Operations- The work that goes into maintaining a fully operationally cloud.
Evidence- a notable event that could verified in operations. 
Escalation- Bringing a problem higher to someone with the right access, authority and or expertise.
Sandbox- A playground area for the user to experiment within boundaries and restrictions. 
AWS Region- The areas of use permitted within the learner lab. Typically us-east-1 and us-west 2.
Virtualization- removing the need for direct access to the hardware for software defined actions.
Operations Playbook- The record keeping made from tickets to understand when similar problems occur.
Managed Services- A technical model that defines the technical support of the provider and which operational responsibilities lie with the consumer. 
